From: "Qwen (Arena agent)" <agent@arena.local>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:13:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(auth): Resend delivery observability and Redis offline
 mode

Applies Revision 2 addendum sections A1 (catalog extraction), A2 (Resend
delivery bug) and A3 (Redis offline mode) to the shipped Phase 1-7 code.

A2 - Resend delivery contract:
- log the full response {id, status, error} plus the request id on every
  send (info on success, error on failure); never log the recipient
- reclassify a 2xx carrying no id as a failure, not a silent success
- warn-log every path that answers the byte-identical 200 "check your
  email" ack without sending anything: honeypot drop, formTs timing drop,
  per-address issuance window and invite cooldown. The invite-cooldown
  path previously left no trace anywhere at all
- startup guard: FATAL and refuse to boot on a missing RESEND_API_KEY, or
  on a from-domain that is definitively not verified in Resend. An
  uncheckable domain logs FATAL and boots rather than taking the platform
  down over a control-plane blip
- new POST /api/v1/admin/diagnostics/email-test: super admin only,
  rate-limited, audited as EMAIL_DELIVERY_TEST, returns the raw Resend id

A3 - Redis offline mode:
- REDIS_OPTIONAL=auto|always|never. auto is optional outside production
  and required in it. UPSTASH_REDIS_URL stays a vault secret, so there is
  no second source of truth for the connection string
- bounded boot probe (4s) on the connection the app intends to keep:
  unreachable and optional falls back to memory, unreachable and required
  refuses to boot
- memory-redis shim covers every Redis-backed auth feature (magic-link
  single-use and re-issue invalidation, invite cooldown, MFA challenge
  and replay cache, signup OTP, lockout counters, session registry,
  anti-bot counters). app.redis keeps one type, so no call site needed a
  branch and 19 consumers are untouched
- GET /health reports {redis, store}. /healthz and /readyz keep their
  catalog shapes byte-identical, and no redis readiness probe is
  registered offline so a healthy pod is not pulled from traffic
- BullMQ queues refuse jobs loudly offline (log, count, resolve to
  undefined) instead of inventing a job id. Auth mail is inline and
  unaffected
- single-instance caveat logged on every offline boot and documented

A1 - playbook.md gains the catalog extraction for all five parts (with
the reading method and its coverage limits declared), the Email Delivery
and Redis Mode sections, the A4 Definition-of-Done delta, the Revision 2
decisions and the Known Gaps.

No live Resend send and no live Redis re-enable were performed: this
environment has no RESEND_API_KEY, no dashboard or inbox access, and no
Redis server. Both are recorded in Known Gaps and handed to the user
rather than claimed as done.

Tests: 1048 passed (58 files), up from a 1017/55 baseline - 31 new tests,
zero regressions. tsc --noEmit and eslint clean on every changed file.
